Package: ldaR6
Type: Package
Title: Predictive Linear Discriminant Analysis with R6 and a Shiny Interface
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Chancy Loïc Franlly", family = "MAMPOUYA CLARK", email = "clarkfranlly@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Predictive linear discriminant analysis (LDA) implemented from
    scratch as an 'R6' class with a scikit-learn like interface (fit, predict,
    predict_proba, transform). The core relies on pooled within-class
    covariance matrices and reproduces the classification functions of SAS
    PROC DISCRIM. The package provides Wilks' lambda and Rao's F tests, partial
    (per-variable) contribution tests, stepwise variable selection (forward,
    backward, both) based on Wilks' lambda, automatic handling of categorical
    predictors (dummy, one-hot or label encoding), optional covariance
    shrinkage for high-dimensional data, cross-validation, canonical
    (discriminant) axes, and a Shiny application for beginners.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0)
Imports: R6, stats, graphics, grDevices, utils
Suggests: shiny, bslib, DT, ggplot2, readxl, testthat (>= 3.0.0), MASS,
    knitr, rmarkdown, microbenchmark
Config/testthat/edition: 3
